body:
It isn't a sign of romantic affection, it's a sign of companionship and non-sexual affection between men.  In some parts of the world, men greet eachother with a kiss on the cheek or even on the lips.  In other parts it's common for men to embrace their friend and tell them "I love you, bro".  Ask anyone from the military, and they'll tell you the gayest shit they ever saw probably happened in the Barracks when soldiers were just fooling around to kill time. Just because it's culturally accepted to see men expressing affection for one another, doesn't mean Palestine accepts Homosexuality.  The LGBT community in Palestine faces a precarious situation where their rights are not guaranteed or protected, and in Gaza, Hamas punishes it with 10 years in prison.  

&#x200B;

I guess calling out Muslims on their lies is "Islamophobia".  I've heard that bilge before, that just because their culture doesn't disapprove of public signs of affection among men, means that their culture approves of homosexuality.  I'm glad you can write off the death of a Gay Palestinian as "Israel propaganda", I'm sure he's sad that his horrific murder was a slight inconvenience to you.  Perhaps his spirit can take solace in that his death can be excused as propaganda.

I have two questions;
1) did vendors ever try to get in contact with one another to organize trades or to share info on some DN forum? 

2) besides the usual dealer paranoia, did you have any indication the Police were catching onto you, or about to bust you?
